// BT-3054: exercises `self superclass` (backed by
// beamtalk_behaviour_intrinsics:classSuperclass/1, which calls
// beamtalk_object_class:module_name_safe/1) inside a block that executes in
// a foreign class's process (ADR 0109) — same shape as bt3052parent.bt's
// `self new class`, but for the classSuperclass/1 call site migrated to
// module_name_safe/1 in this PR rather than class_of_object_by_name/1
// (BT-3052's own fix). `self` here is the class object itself
// (closure-captured via `ClassSelf`, per BT-3047).
//
// BT-3057: the corresponding test originally compared the result to the
// Symbol `#BT3047Ancestor` rather than the class object `BT3047Ancestor`,
// because a class-object (`#beamtalk_object{}`) returned out of a class
// method via `self superclass` degraded to a bare Symbol independent of
// this fixture's own changes. BT-3057 fixed that self-send path, so the
// test now compares against the real class object.

BT3047Ancestor subclass: BT3054Parent

  class makeSelfSuperclassThrough: aDriverClass over: aList :: List =>
    aDriverClass
      run: [:x |
        result := self superclass
        ^result
      ]
      over: aList
    #wrong
